**16:10 – JK**
@SB @MP good to hear. I'll update the job board and make sure the permits are printed and in the folder. Do we need to send a copy to control before we leave?

---

**16:12 – SB**
@JK yes, control wants a copy of the approved WO with the site plan attached. I'll email it through before I lock up. Can you make sure the site plan is the latest version? I think there was a revision last week.

---

**16:13 – JK**
@SB will do. I'll check the revision date on the drawings and grab the latest from the server. Won't take long.

---

**16:15 – KP**
@SB quick question – does the approval cover the full scope or just the first phase? I remember we discussed splitting it into two stages if the weather turned.

---

**16:16 – SB**
@KP full scope, no split. The WO covers everything we planned for the two days. But we'll still do the usual stop-go decision if conditions change, so don't worry about that.

---

**16:18 – MP**
@KP I think we're all set then. I'll do the final truck check now and make sure the tool list is complete. Anyone need anything specific from the store before I head off?

---

**16:19 – TD**
@MP I could use a couple of extra warning lights if there are any in the store. The ones on the truck are a bit dim from the last job. Just in case we're working near the crossing.

---

**16:20 – MP**
@TD I'll have a look. If I find them, I'll chuck them in the back and let you know.

---

**16:22 – SB**
@MP thanks. Also, if anyone has the old risk assessment for the north end signal work, can you bring it to the briefing? I want to compare it with the new one to make sure we haven't missed anything.

---

**16:24 – TD**
@SB I've got a copy from the last time we did that area. I'll bring it along, no worries.

---

**16:26 – JK**
@SB @TD good. I'll bring the updated one from the server, so we'll have both to check against.

---

Sarah approved_work_order WO-2026-0811-03. Record status: current.

**16:28 – KP**
@SB just to confirm, the approved WO number is WO-2026-0811-03, right? I want to make sure I'm referencing the right one in the logbook.

---

**16:29 – SB**
@KP yes, that's the one. Current and valid for this job. I'll post the reference in the thread header as well so we don't lose it.

---

**16:31 – MP**
@SB @KP noted. I've updated the truck checklist with the WO number as well, so we're all on the same page.

---

**16:33 – TD**
@MP cheers. I'll do the same with the site drawings – just put the WO number on the cover sheet so it matches the paperwork.

---

**16:35 – SB**
@all I'm heading to the office to send the paperwork to control and lock up. If anything comes up, call me on the radio or leave a message here and I'll get back to you.

---

**16:37 – JK**
@SB thanks for sorting that. I'll see everyone at the briefing at 17:00 then.

---

**16:38 – MP**
@JK see you there. I'll be at the truck doing the final checks until then.

---

**16:40 – KP**
@SB one more thing – do we need to bring the spare radios or are the ones from the last job still charged? I don't want to be short on comms if we split up on site.

---

**16:41 – SB**
@KP the radios from last job are still in the charging dock in the office. I'll leave them there for you. Just grab them on your way out.

---

**16:42 – KP**
@SB perfect, thanks. I'll grab them before I leave.

---

**16:44 – TD**
@SB also, if you're locking up, can you check if the first aid kit in the office is fully stocked? I used a couple of bandages last week and I'm not sure if they've been replaced.

**16:46 – MP**
@TD good call. I think there's a spare box of bandages in the top drawer of the filing cabinet. Can you grab it and top it up before you leave?

---

**16:48 – TD**
@MP will do. I'll check the kit and restock it now.

---

**16:50 – SB**
@all I'm off to the office now. I'll send the paperwork and lock up. See everyone at the briefing.

---

**16:52 – JK**
@SB cheers. I'll head over to the shed to grab the updated drawings and meet you at the office.

---

**16:55 – MP**
@JK I'll be at the truck doing final checks. If you need me, give me a shout on the radio.

---

**16:57 – TD**
@MP just finished restocking the first aid kit. All good now.

---

**17:00 – JK**
@all Briefing starting now in the office. Everyone here?

---

**17:02 – MP**
@JK on my way. Just locking up the truck.

---

**17:04 – KP**
@JK I'm here. Already in the office.

---

**17:06 – SB**
@JK I'm here too. Ready to start.

---

**17:08 – TD**
@JK just arrived. Sorry for the delay, had to finish up the first aid kit.

---

**17:10 – JK**
@all Good, we're all here. Let's get started.

---

**17:15 – JK**
@all Briefing notes:
- WO-2026-0811-03 approved and current
- Site: TS-9, SB-12, OH-7
- Bring both old and new drawings to compare
- Radios charged and in the office
- First aid kit restocked

---

**17:20 – SB**
@JK thanks for the summary. I'll send the paperwork to control now.

---

**17:22 – MP**
@JK I've got the updated drawings with me. I'll bring them to the site.

---

**17:25 – TD**
@JK I'll take the old drawings. We'll compare them on site.

---

**17:28 – KP**
@JK I've got the spare radios. I'll bring them along.

---

**17:30 – JK**
@all Great. Let's aim to leave by 17:45. I'll do a final check on the truck and then we're off.

---

**17:32 – MP**
@JK I'll do the final truck check now. Everything looks good so far.

---

**17:35 – TD**
@MP let me know if you need a hand with anything.

---

**17:38 – MP**
@TD thanks, I think we're all set. Just checking the lights and brakes.

---

**17:40 – JK**
@all Remember to bring your radios and the drawings. I'll see you at the truck in 5.

---

**17:42 – KP**
@JK got the radios. On my way.

---

**17:45 – JK**
@all Everyone ready? Let's head out.

---

**17:47 – MP**
@JK all good here. Let's go.

---

**17:50 – TD**
@JK ready when you are.

---

**17:52 – SB**
@JK I'll stay back and lock up the office. I'll catch up with you at the site later.

---

**17:55 – JK**
@SB sounds good. We'll see you there.

---

**18:00 – JK**
@all We're heading to the site now. ETA about 18:20. I'll update you when we arrive.

---

**18:05 – MP**
@JK copy that. I'll be on the radio if you need anything.

---

**18:10 – TD**
@JK just checking the weather forecast for the site. Looks clear for the next few hours.

---

**18:12 – JK**
@TD good to know. Thanks for checking.

---

**18:15 – KP**
@JK I've got the site access keys with me. We'll be able to get in without any issues.

---

**18:18 – JK**
@KP perfect. I was worried about that. Thanks.

---

**18:20 – JK**
@all We've arrived at the site. Starting the initial assessment now.

---

**18:25 – MP**
@JK I'll start setting up the safety barriers while you do the assessment.

---

**18:28 – TD**
@JK I'll take a look at the old drawings and compare them with the new ones to see if there are any differences.

---

**18:30 – KP**
@JK I'll check the radios and make sure we have good communication across the site.

**18:35 – JK**
@all Initial assessment is done. The main issue is the same one we flagged in the report – the drainage culvert under the crossing is partially blocked. We'll need to clear it before the rain forecast for tomorrow afternoon. I'll send through the full notes when we get back.

---

**18:40 – MP**
@JK the barriers are up on both approaches. I'll do a quick walk of the site to make sure there's nothing else that needs attention.

---

**18:42 – TD**
@JK I compared the old and new drawings side by side. The only real difference is the position of the signal cable duct – it's about 2 metres further east on the new plan. That shouldn't affect the culvert work but it's worth noting for the record.

---

**18:45 – KP**
@TD good catch. I'll add that to the notes. Radios are all working, we've got clear comms across the whole site.

---

**18:48 – JK**
@all OK, here's the plan for the next hour. We'll clear the culvert, check the drainage pipe for any cracks, and then do a final inspection of the crossing surface. If we find anything else, we'll flag it immediately.

---

**18:50 – MP**
@JK sounds good. I'll start on the culvert clearing now. Do we have the right tools on the truck?

---

**18:52 – JK**
@MP I believe so. I packed the shovels and the crowbar. If we need anything else, we can radio back to base.

---

**18:55 – TD**
@JK I'll do a visual check of the drainage pipe while you clear the culvert. That way we can cover both at once.

---

**18:58 – KP**
@JK I'll stay on the radio and coordinate with base if anything comes up.

---

**19:00 – JK**
@all Let's get to it. I'll be at the culvert with MP. TD, you've got the pipe. KP, you're on comms.

---

**19:05 – MP**
@JK started clearing the culvert. It's pretty clogged with leaves and mud. Might take a bit longer than expected.

---

**19:10 – TD**
@JK the pipe looks clear from what I can see. No obvious cracks. I'll do a closer inspection once you're done with the culvert.

---

**19:15 – JK**
@MP keep at it. We've got time before the weather turns. Let me know if you need a hand.

---

**19:20 – MP**
@JK I think I've got the worst of it out. Just a bit more to go.

---

**19:25 – KP**
@all base just called. They want an update on our progress. I'll tell them we're on track for the planned finish time.

---

**19:30 – JK**
@KP good. Let them know we're roughly halfway through the clearing and the pipe inspection is going well.

---

**19:35 – TD**
@JK I've finished the pipe inspection. No damage found. The drainage looks fine once the culvert is clear.

---

**19:40 – MP**
@JK culvert is clear. I'm just doing a final check on the crossing surface now.

---

**19:45 – JK**
@MP excellent. Let me know if you see anything concerning.

---

**19:50 – MP**
@JK surface looks good. No major cracks or issues. I think we're done here.

---

**19:55 – JK**
@all Great work everyone. I'll do a final walkthrough of the site to make sure everything is in order, then we'll pack up and head back.

---

**20:00 – TD**
@JK I'll start packing up the tools and the barriers while you do the walkthrough.

---

**20:05 – KP**
@JK I'll do a final radio check and then we can head out.

---

**20:10 – JK**
@all Site is all clear. Good job team. Let's pack up and get back to the depot.

---

**20:15 – MP**
@JK done with the barriers. I'll load them on the truck.

---

**20:18 – TD**
@JK tools are packed. I'll help MP with the barriers.

**20:25 – MP**
@JK all loaded up. Truck is ready when you are.

---

**20:30 – JK**
@all good work tonight. Sign off sheets are on the clipboard in the office. Please make sure you fill them in before you head off.

---

**20:32 – TD**
@JK done. Signed off already.

---

**20:35 – KP**
@JK signed off too. Radio gear is back in the charging rack.

---

**20:40 – MP**
@JK done. See you all tmrw.

---

**20:45 – JK**
@all cheers team. I'll file the report with Central Control and then we're done for the night.

---

**11 Aug 2026 – Morning**

**06:15 – KP**
@all morning. Weather update for today: fine and dry, high of 24°C. No issues expected for the day shift. The overnight culvert work went well, no follow-up needed.

---

**06:20 – JK**
@KP thanks. Can you confirm the next possession window is still on for tomorrow night? I want to make sure we havent missed anything.

---

**06:22 – KP**
@JK yes, MW-2026-08-12 is confirmed. Start time 21:00, as per the weekly plan. I'll send the updated work order to your email shortly.

---

**06:25 – JK**
@KP good. I'll start prepping the crew and equipment list for that one today.

---

**06:30 – MP**
@all morning. I'll be in around 07:00. Need to do a quick check on the grinder before we take it out tmrw. It was making a odd noise last week.

---

**06:32 – TD**
@MP I can take a look at it with you if you want. I'm coming in early too.

---

**06:35 – MP**
@TD sounds good. Meet you at the workshop.

---

**06:40 – JK**
@all Just a heads up: the rail grinder is booked for the MW-2026-08-12 possession. If it's not ready, we'll need to swap in the backup unit. Let me know by end of shift today if theres an issue.

---

**06:45 – MP**
@JK will do. We'll have an answer by lunch.

---

**07:10 – MP**
@TD got the grinder open. Looks like a worn bearing on the drive shaft. I've got a replacement in the parts store. Should be able to fix it this morning.

---

**07:15 – TD**
@MP good find. I'll grab the torque wrench and we can get it sorted.

---

**07:20 – KP**
@all base just sent through the final crew list for MW-2026-08-12. Confirming the following: JK (coordinator), MP, TD, and myself. That's 4 people total. Please confirm you're all available.

---

**07:22 – MP**
@KP confirmed.

---

**07:23 – TD**
@KP confirmed.

---

**07:25 – JK**
@KP confirmed. I'll be there.

---

**07:26 – KP**
@all all confirmed. I'll send the list back to base.

---

**07:30 – JK**
@all Equipment check for tmrw night:
- Rail grinder (being repaired, see MP/TD)
- Angle grinder with cutting discs
- Spare blades
- Welding kit (check gas levels)
- Hi-vis vests and hard hats (everyone has their own?)
- Portable radios (KP to charge)
- Warning lights and barriers (MP to load)
- First aid kit (TD to check expiry)

Let me know if anything is missing or needs attention.

---

**07:35 – TD**
@JK first aid kit is good, expires next month. I'll bring it tmrw.

---

**07:40 – MP**
@JK I'll grab the barriers and lights from the storage shed this arvo and load them on the truck so we're ready to go.

---

**07:45 – KP**
@JK radios are on charge now. I'll do a full check this afternoon.

---

**07:50 – JK**
@all thanks team. Looks like we're on track. I'll do a final review of the work order after lunch and share the details.

---

**08:15 – MP**
@JK grinder is fixed. New bearing installed and tested, runs smooth now. We're good to go for tmrw.

---

**08:20 – JK**
@MP excellent. Thanks for the quick turnaround. I'll update the equipment list.
